WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.320
- I'm announcing the first
tranche of sanctions.

00:00:02.320 --> 00:00:05.110
- These sanctions are a major step.

00:00:05.110 --> 00:00:07.919
- And we hold further
sanctions at readiness

00:00:07.919 --> 00:00:09.460
to be deployed.

00:00:09.460 --> 00:00:11.800
- This is about as close
to global economic war

00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:12.780
as we've ever come.

00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:15.520
- Compared to all historical campaigns,

00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:17.560
this is staking sanctions to the limit.

00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:18.930
- The economy is tanking,

00:00:18.930 --> 00:00:21.150
the ruble has fallen through the floor.

00:00:21.150 --> 00:00:23.330
Inflation is soaring.

00:00:23.330 --> 00:00:25.090
Interest rates are up.

00:00:25.090 --> 00:00:27.440
- [Narrator] The Russian
invasion of Ukraine triggered

00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:29.130
a global economic response

00:00:29.130 --> 00:00:30.640
without precedent in terms

00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:32.960
of its speed, scale and scope.

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:35.810
- The sanctions we
imposed have generated 2/3

00:00:35.810 --> 00:00:37.330
of the world joining us.

00:00:37.330 --> 00:00:39.200
They are profound sanctions.

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:41.040
- The European Union and its partners

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:43.690
are working to cripple Putin's ability

00:00:43.690 --> 00:00:46.080
to finance his war machine.

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:47.360
- [Narrator] In a matter of days,

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:50.220
the US, the UK, the EU and others

00:00:50.220 --> 00:00:53.620
essentially unplugged the
world's 11th largest economy

00:00:53.620 --> 00:00:55.460
from the global economic system.

00:00:55.460 --> 00:00:58.520
- We have never applied such deep, severe

00:00:58.520 --> 00:01:02.540
and far-reaching sanctions
on such a large country.

00:01:02.540 --> 00:01:05.400
Vladimir Putin himself has
called it a declaration of war

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:07.260
and in economic terms, he's not far off.

00:01:07.260 --> 00:01:09.330
- [Narrator] But will
this financial assault

00:01:09.330 --> 00:01:12.280
on the Russian economy
actually achieve its goal

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:14.540
of pressuring Russian
President Vladimir Putin

00:01:14.540 --> 00:01:16.430
to call off his troops?

00:01:16.430 --> 00:01:17.910
- The big gamble right now

00:01:17.910 --> 00:01:21.750
is to see if the West can
bankrupt Russia enough

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:23.740
that they cannot fight an insurgency.

00:01:23.740 --> 00:01:25.930
- [Narrator] Moreover, what
will be the consequences

00:01:25.930 --> 00:01:28.490
of this economic war
for everyday Russians?

00:01:28.490 --> 00:01:31.280
And how will this conflict
affect the US economy

00:01:31.280 --> 00:01:33.563
and the lives of everyday Americans?

00:01:35.230 --> 00:01:39.530
In 1990, just months after
the fall of the Berlin Wall,

00:01:39.530 --> 00:01:42.220
Russia's first McDonald's
opened in Moscow,

00:01:42.220 --> 00:01:45.480
a sign that the nation was
joining the global economy.

00:01:45.480 --> 00:01:47.310
But on March 8th of this year,

00:01:47.310 --> 00:01:49.590
the chain announced that
it would be closing all

00:01:49.590 --> 00:01:52.380
of its restaurants in Russia temporarily.

00:01:52.380 --> 00:01:54.190
- It definitely feels
like a new Iron Curtain

00:01:54.190 --> 00:01:55.780
is coming down between East and West.

00:01:55.780 --> 00:01:57.610
I mean, back during the Cold War,

00:01:57.610 --> 00:01:58.853
it was taken for granted
that the Soviet bloc

00:01:58.853 --> 00:02:01.460
and the Western bloc did
not trade with each other

00:02:01.460 --> 00:02:04.080
and we're in some sense
returning to that world.

00:02:04.080 --> 00:02:06.990
- [Narrator] The first move
was made by Western governments

00:02:06.990 --> 00:02:09.070
when they targeted Russia's banking system

00:02:09.070 --> 00:02:11.040
by blocking the Russian Central Bank

00:02:11.040 --> 00:02:13.580
from selling its foreign
currency reserves.

00:02:13.580 --> 00:02:17.200
- We will stop Putin
from using his war chest.

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:19.440
- Perhaps the most severe impact

00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:21.600
has been the seizing of the assets

00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:22.940
of the Central Bank of Russia.

00:02:22.940 --> 00:02:26.090
Basically, Putin put away a lot of money

00:02:26.090 --> 00:02:29.930
for a rainy day to help
him weather the storms

00:02:29.930 --> 00:02:32.552
of future sanctions episodes.

00:02:32.552 --> 00:02:37.552
(Vladimir speaking in foreign language)

00:02:37.630 --> 00:02:38.780
- [Narrator] Sanctions sent the value

00:02:38.780 --> 00:02:41.770
of the ruble to an all-time
low against the dollar.

00:02:41.770 --> 00:02:44.230
Prices for Russia's
most important exports,

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:48.350
like natural gas, nickel and
wheat shot up to record highs.

00:02:48.350 --> 00:02:53.140
The US, the EU, the UK and
Canada removed some Russian banks

00:02:53.140 --> 00:02:56.180
from SWFIT, the financial
messaging network used

00:02:56.180 --> 00:02:58.010
by banks across the globe.

00:02:58.010 --> 00:03:00.540
Additional sanctions included blacklisting

00:03:00.540 --> 00:03:03.580
Russia's biggest banks from
the global financial system,

00:03:03.580 --> 00:03:06.770
legislation to freeze Russian
oligarch wealth abroad.

00:03:06.770 --> 00:03:09.530
- This is not an economic crime bill,

00:03:09.530 --> 00:03:11.280
it's an economic warfare bill.

00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:12.760
- [Narrator] And export restrictions

00:03:12.760 --> 00:03:15.060
for certain technologies.

00:03:15.060 --> 00:03:17.120
- We estimate that we'll
cut off more than half

00:03:17.120 --> 00:03:19.070
of Russia's high-tech imports.

00:03:19.070 --> 00:03:21.100
- [Narrator] This economic
war may have begun

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:22.490
with government sanctions

00:03:22.490 --> 00:03:24.180
but as the conflict has continued,

00:03:24.180 --> 00:03:26.160
private companies and investors

00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:29.060
have begun to voluntarily
sever ties with Russian.

00:03:29.060 --> 00:03:32.200
- Many Western companies,
without being forced to,

00:03:32.200 --> 00:03:35.130
are simply packing up and leaving Russia.

00:03:35.130 --> 00:03:37.970
We're seeing, even though in
theory Russian oil and gas

00:03:37.970 --> 00:03:39.273
is exempt from sanctions,

00:03:39.273 --> 00:03:42.900
many market participants simply don't want

00:03:42.900 --> 00:03:45.220
to do business with Russian oil and gas.

00:03:45.220 --> 00:03:46.950
- [Narrator] Some
Western companies decided

00:03:46.950 --> 00:03:49.170
to suspend operations in Russia,

00:03:49.170 --> 00:03:51.924
while others decided to pull out entirely.

00:03:51.924 --> 00:03:56.591
(Vladimir speaking in foreign language)

00:04:04.400 --> 00:04:05.650
- [Narrator] For everyday Russians,

00:04:05.650 --> 00:04:07.900
the sanctions can be seen in emptier shops

00:04:07.900 --> 00:04:11.050
as foreign brands and businesses
pause their operations

00:04:11.050 --> 00:04:13.300
or exit the country entirely.

00:04:13.300 --> 00:04:14.495
There's also bank runs

00:04:14.495 --> 00:04:17.650
as those with deposits
in foreign currency rush

00:04:17.650 --> 00:04:20.130
to take it out or convert
their rubles to dollars

00:04:20.130 --> 00:04:22.150
to protect the value of their savings.

00:04:22.150 --> 00:04:23.530
- Imagine that you had a bank account full

00:04:23.530 --> 00:04:25.000
of money and you said, well,

00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:26.940
there's all the money I
need to buy my groceries,

00:04:26.940 --> 00:04:29.510
put gas in my car, to
pay my mortgage bill.

00:04:29.510 --> 00:04:30.627
And then one day the government said,

00:04:30.627 --> 00:04:32.220
"I'm sorry, you have all that money

00:04:32.220 --> 00:04:33.387
but we're not gonna let
you have access it."

00:04:33.387 --> 00:04:34.640
What's gonna happen?

00:04:34.640 --> 00:04:36.690
Well, you're gonna starve,
your car's gonna run out of gas

00:04:36.690 --> 00:04:38.390
and you're gonna default on your mortgage

00:04:38.390 --> 00:04:40.120
and that is more or less
what's happening to Russia

00:04:40.120 --> 00:04:41.780
on kind of a macro scale.

00:04:41.780 --> 00:04:43.890
- [Narrator] Russian
bond prices also sank.

00:04:43.890 --> 00:04:46.300
The country's dollar-denominated
sovereign bonds

00:04:46.300 --> 00:04:49.530
were quoted at around 17 cents
on the dollar on March 2nd,

00:04:49.530 --> 00:04:52.320
down from 95 cents the previous week.

00:04:52.320 --> 00:04:54.690
- It is more or less being shoved

00:04:54.690 --> 00:04:57.000
into the financial
equivalent of the Stone Age.

00:04:57.000 --> 00:05:00.000
- You'll see over the coming
weeks that a global economy,

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:01.800
a Western-oriented economy,

00:05:01.800 --> 00:05:04.880
a relatively well-off middle class economy

00:05:04.880 --> 00:05:07.810
is gonna see its livelihood be wiped out.

00:05:07.810 --> 00:05:09.180
- [Narrator] Although
Russia will bear the brunt

00:05:09.180 --> 00:05:10.280
of these sanctions,

00:05:10.280 --> 00:05:13.300
their impact is already
being felt across the world.

00:05:13.300 --> 00:05:14.800
- You don't cut yourself off from one

00:05:14.800 --> 00:05:16.300
of the world's largest exporters

00:05:16.300 --> 00:05:18.930
of oil and gas and other
valuable commodities overnight

00:05:18.930 --> 00:05:20.580
and expect there to be no effect.

00:05:20.580 --> 00:05:23.290
- [Narrator] This month, the
price for brent crude oil

00:05:23.290 --> 00:05:24.650
hit a record high.

00:05:24.650 --> 00:05:26.790
- Today I'm announcing the United States

00:05:26.790 --> 00:05:29.690
is targeting the main
artery of Russia's economy.

00:05:29.690 --> 00:05:31.650
- [Narrator] The Biden
administration banned the import

00:05:31.650 --> 00:05:34.670
of Russian oil, though the
US only imports about 8%

00:05:34.670 --> 00:05:36.433
of its oil from Russia.

00:05:36.433 --> 00:05:41.100
(Vladimir speaking in foreign language)

00:05:58.400 --> 00:06:01.220
- [Narrator] Russia
produces 11% of global oil

00:06:01.220 --> 00:06:04.430
and possesses 25% of the
world's natural gas reserves,

00:06:04.430 --> 00:06:05.870
so cutting those resources off

00:06:05.870 --> 00:06:09.210
from the global economy is
unlikely to happen overnight.

00:06:09.210 --> 00:06:10.130
That's especially true

00:06:10.130 --> 00:06:12.600
for Russia's biggest natural
gas customer, Europe,

00:06:12.600 --> 00:06:14.940
which relies on Russia for about 40%

00:06:14.940 --> 00:06:16.440
of its natural gas.

00:06:16.440 --> 00:06:18.280
- And that's the big question mark.

00:06:18.280 --> 00:06:20.160
Who's gonna touch gas first?

00:06:20.160 --> 00:06:21.500
It's a third rail.

00:06:21.500 --> 00:06:22.640
Will Europe do it

00:06:22.640 --> 00:06:26.440
and say we're gonna take the
economic costs no matter what?

00:06:26.440 --> 00:06:28.470
- Putin could preempt that

00:06:28.470 --> 00:06:32.490
and stop shipments of
oil and gas to Europe.

00:06:32.490 --> 00:06:34.970
That would have a dramatic impact

00:06:34.970 --> 00:06:36.778
on European economies

00:06:36.778 --> 00:06:40.440
but it would also mean
that no money is flow

00:06:40.440 --> 00:06:43.350
or hardly any money is
flowing into Russia anymore.

00:06:43.350 --> 00:06:45.650
- [Narrator] Russia's also
the world's largest exporter

00:06:45.650 --> 00:06:47.870
of wheat, a major exporter of coal

00:06:47.870 --> 00:06:51.320
and one of the top producers
of metals and fertilizer.

00:06:51.320 --> 00:06:53.530
- How are we gonna
replace that grain, right?

00:06:53.530 --> 00:06:54.550
How are we gonna make sure

00:06:54.550 --> 00:06:56.880
that North Africa and the
Middle East don't starve

00:06:56.880 --> 00:06:58.160
as a result of this?

00:06:58.160 --> 00:06:59.270
- [Narrator] Sanctions are supposed

00:06:59.270 --> 00:07:01.600
to compel a country to change its behavior

00:07:01.600 --> 00:07:03.690
but some experts say these economic tools

00:07:03.690 --> 00:07:05.560
don't always accomplish their goals.

00:07:05.560 --> 00:07:06.890
- I think it could backfire.

00:07:06.890 --> 00:07:07.723
Yeah.

00:07:07.723 --> 00:07:09.310
- [Narrator] Julia
Friedlander says historically

00:07:09.310 --> 00:07:10.143
they've rarely forced

00:07:10.143 --> 00:07:12.680
the targeted country
to change its behavior.

00:07:12.680 --> 00:07:14.680
- If your goal is to stop a war,

00:07:14.680 --> 00:07:16.750
to stop Putin from flattening Ukraine

00:07:16.750 --> 00:07:19.580
using financial means, then you may lose.

00:07:19.580 --> 00:07:21.930
Putin tomorrow could flatten Ukraine

00:07:21.930 --> 00:07:23.090
through aerial bombardment

00:07:23.090 --> 00:07:24.720
and then sanctions would
have meant nothing.

00:07:24.720 --> 00:07:26.730
We might come to see that these sanctions

00:07:26.730 --> 00:07:27.960
were not worth it.

00:07:27.960 --> 00:07:30.264
That all of the effort that we expended

00:07:30.264 --> 00:07:33.935
actually caused more crisis
than we had reckoned with.

00:07:33.935 --> 00:07:36.000
(dramatic music)

00:07:36.000 --> 00:07:37.000
- [Narrator] In some cases,

00:07:37.000 --> 00:07:39.430
sanctions have hastened global conflict

00:07:39.430 --> 00:07:40.540
rather than ending it.

00:07:40.540 --> 00:07:42.350
- If you go back in history,

00:07:42.350 --> 00:07:44.250
you can find the sanctions

00:07:44.250 --> 00:07:48.640
or oil embargo against Japan
pushed the Japanese regime

00:07:48.640 --> 00:07:52.418
into a corner and led them
to respond militarily.

00:07:52.418 --> 00:07:54.220
And we got Pearl Harbor.

00:07:54.220 --> 00:07:55.270
- [Narrator] On March 16th,

00:07:55.270 --> 00:07:57.270
Fed Chairman Jerome Powell announced

00:07:57.270 --> 00:07:59.630
that the central bank would
be hiking interest rates

00:07:59.630 --> 00:08:01.160
to curb rising inflation,

00:08:01.160 --> 00:08:03.550
which is being exacerbated by the war.

00:08:03.550 --> 00:08:05.310
- The surge in prices of crude oil

00:08:05.310 --> 00:08:06.930
and other commodities that resulted

00:08:06.930 --> 00:08:08.696
from Russia's invasion of Ukraine

00:08:08.696 --> 00:08:11.100
will put additional upward pressure

00:08:11.100 --> 00:08:13.230
on near-term inflation here at home.

00:08:13.230 --> 00:08:16.211
- The American government can take steps

00:08:16.211 --> 00:08:19.810
to help manage and assuage some

00:08:19.810 --> 00:08:23.900
of the pain that is being felt

00:08:23.900 --> 00:08:27.840
by those that are affected most directly

00:08:27.840 --> 00:08:30.130
by the increased energy costs.

00:08:30.130 --> 00:08:32.130
- Right now there is extraordinary support

00:08:32.130 --> 00:08:34.300
across the West for these sanctions

00:08:34.300 --> 00:08:35.970
and for the Ukrainian people.

00:08:35.970 --> 00:08:38.010
It is not clear that six months from now

00:08:38.010 --> 00:08:41.240
after a period of very
painfully high prices

00:08:41.240 --> 00:08:42.650
and perhaps weaker economic growth

00:08:42.650 --> 00:08:44.450
if that support will still be there.

